# Documentation

## Purpose

Keep the docs site (and in-code docs) consistent, discoverable, and in sync with the public API.

## Why it exists

`packages/docs` is the public VitePress site consumers rely on. Every new adapter/handler or
public behavior change must be documented and wired into navigation, or users cannot find it.

## Stack & structure

- VitePress with a near-stock theme; config in `packages/docs/.vitepress/config.mts`
  (`themeConfig.sidebar`, `nav`, `socialLinks`, `sitemap`).
- Folders MIRROR the sidebar groups: `getting-started/`, `adapters/<framework>/`, `handlers/`
  (the "Watchers" sidebar section), `ui-interaction.md`. Adding a page WITHOUT adding its
  sidebar entry in `config.mts` is incomplete.
- Terminology: the docs section is "Watchers" but the folder/aggregator pages say "handlers"
  (the `@lensjs/watchers` package) — the terms are interchangeable; keep matching existing pages.

## Frontmatter

Use frontmatter only when needed: `layout: home` (`index.md`), `outline: deep` (long pages).
Most content pages have no frontmatter — do not add boilerplate.

## Tone & structure

- Second person, friendly, task-oriented.
- Numbered H2 step sections (`## 1. Install Packages`, `## 2. Minimal Setup`,
  `## 3. Next Steps`). Recurring sections: Prerequisites, Usage Example, Try it out,
  Next Steps, Custom Handlers, Configuration.
- Bold product/framework names and key toggles; cross-link with relative `.md` links.

## Code blocks

- Always tag the language: ` ```ts `, ` ```bash `, ` ```mermaid `.
- Use VitePress code features where helpful (`// [!code ++]`, `// [!code --]`, `// ...` to elide
  boilerplate); keep the primary path copy-pasteable.
- CONSUMER docs install with `npm` (`npm install @lensjs/watchers`); CONTRIBUTOR docs use
  `pnpm`. Do not mix.

## Recipe: documenting a new adapter or handler

- New adapter: add `adapters/<framework>/installation.md` (+ `configuration.md`); register a
  collapsed group under "Adapters" in `config.mts`. Follow the express pages' shape (install ->
  minimal setup -> "Try it out" -> configuration with all options inline-commented).
- New handler: add `handlers/<signal>/<framework>.md`; register it under the matching signal
  sub-group in the "Watchers" sidebar. Restate the `QueryWatcherHandler` contract in a
  "Custom Handlers" section.

## In-code documentation

- Add JSDoc to exported utility functions, mirroring
  [utils/exception.ts](mdc:packages/core/src/utils/exception.ts) and
  [utils/index.ts](mdc:packages/core/src/utils/index.ts).
- Do not write comments that restate code; document intent/constraints only (see `typescript.mdc`).

## AI must never

- Add a docs page without wiring it into the `config.mts` sidebar.
- Document an API shape that does not match the actual code (verify against source before
  writing examples).
- Use `pnpm` in consumer-facing install snippets, or invent options a package does not accept.
